  "description": "<p>This is essentially the same as issue \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-1102\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-1102\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"URL Escaping PIDs Returns 404s\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10303?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-1102\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n.</p>\n\n<p>When 1102 was fixed in <a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/commit/2aa71e3db6f2aba5b66b22783594b035fbe0119d\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/commit/2aa71e3db6f2aba5b66b22783594b035fbe0119d</a> the VALID_PID_PART regular expression constant was added to FedoraObjectsResource and DatastreamResource, but the original (problematic) regular expression is still present in RelationshipResource. </p>\n\n<p>Currently it uses (<span class=\"error\">&#91;A-Za-z0-9&#93;</span>|<del>|<br class=\"atl-forced-newline\" />.)+<img class=\"emoticon\" src=\"/images/icons/emoticons/sad.png\" height=\"16\" width=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" border=\"0\"/>(<span class=\"error\">&#91;A-Za-z0-9&#93;</span>)|</del>|<br class=\"atl-forced-newline\" />.|~|_|(%<span class=\"error\">&#91;0-9A-F&#93;</span></p>\n{2}\n<p>))+ which matches \"test:1234\" but not \"test:%3a1234\" (see <a href=\"http://fiddle.re/pp0m\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://fiddle.re/pp0m</a> ). The VALID_PID_PART regular expression correctly matches either PID.</p>",
